WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:02.640
Mind your decisions, I'm Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:07.139
Simplify the following expression: log base 2 of 3,

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:14.300
multiplied by log base 3 of 4, multiplied by log base 4 of 5, and so on, until the final term,

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.460
log base 127 of 128.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:21.320
I adapted this problem from a post I saw on Reddit homework help.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:30.680
Pause if you'd like to give this problem a try, and when you're ready, keep watching to learn how to solve this problem.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.920
Recall the change of base formula for logarithms:

00:00:44.469 --> 00:00:50.309
Log base b of u is equal to log base a of u divided by log base a of b.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:57.880
This is for u greater than zero (0) and a and b positive real numbers that are not equal to one (1).

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.580
For the special case where a is equal to e,

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.900
we simplify this to the natural log of u (ln u) over the natural log of b (ln b).

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:09.800
We'll use this version of the formula to simplify this product.

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:14.480
The first term becomes the natural log of 3 (ln 3) over the natural log of 2 (ln 2).

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:18.560
The second term becomes the natural log of 4 over the natural log of 3.

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:24.340
We continue to apply this formula all the way to the very end of this product.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:27.560
We then notice an interesting pattern.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:34.980
Natural log of 3 (ln 3) in the numerator of the first term will cancel with natural log of 3 in the denominator of the second term.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:40.380
Then the natural log of 4 will cancel out between the second and third terms,

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:44.080
and this pattern will continue all the way to the very final term.

00:01:44.649 --> 00:01:51.329
The pattern is reminiscent of a retracting telescope where only the very beginning and the very end survived.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:58.829
For this reason it's known as a telescoping product: only the very beginning and the very end survived.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:04.200
We can then simplify this formula one more time using the change of base formula.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:10.040
The natural log of 128 over the natural log of 2 will be equal to log base 2 of 128.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:17.540
128 is equal to 2 to the power 7, and therefore this simplifies to be 7, and that's our answer.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:21.680
I love how this problem miraculously simplifies.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:31.400
Thanks for making Mind Your Decisions one of the best channels on YouTube. As always, thanks for watching and thanks for your support.

